</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_gulf_escalation::vessel_transit_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained fall in commercial transit through the chokepoint reduces the political and operational rationale for allied forward naval and air patrols, lowering visible deterrence and creating conditions in which Russian forces judge they can increase the tempo and severity of kinetic strikes in and around Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_gulf_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_gulf_escalation::vessel_transit_rate" target="us_china_strategic_rival::ai_adoption_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained reductions in commercial vessel transits create immediate upstream shortages and lengthened lead times for servers, GPUs and networking hardware, causing enterprise capex delays and slower rollouts of production AI systems, lowering near‑term adoption rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_gulf_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
</edge>
