<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::ai_infra_concentration" target="global_bond_repricing::market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Greater concentration of AI infrastructure providers increases correlated exposures and single-point operational/counterparty risk across financial firms, which widens bid-ask spreads and reduces depth in bond markets when stress events occur, degrading market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::ai_infra_concentration" target="global_oil_reordering::legal_sanctions_regime_s" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">High concentration of AI compute and cloud infrastructure in a few firms/countries lowers the political and technical cost of crafting precise sanctions, motivating legislators and regulators to broaden legal tools aimed at chokepoints in the AI stack.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">global_oil_reordering</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::ai_infra_concentration" target="russia_ukraine_war::coordination_info_sharin" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Greater concentration of AI infrastructure in a small set of allied providers makes it easier for the U.S. and partners to build interoperable, access-controlled platforms and legal/technical agreements for intelligence and operational data exchange, raising formalized coordination and information-sharing levels.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
