  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in geopolitical conflict in key energy or trade lanes drives a near-term flight-to-quality into core sovereign debt (e.g., US, Germany), pushing prices up and long-term yields down as investors reallocate away from risk assets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_oil_reordering</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_repricing</data>
