  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">A higher prevailing policy short-term rate raises borrowing and debt-servicing costs for regional partners and tightens allied budgetary space, producing shorter-term cuts or slower rotation of naval/patrol deployments that weaken effective maritime control versus Iranian/coercive actors.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_escalation</data>
