  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in long-term sovereign yields increases Russia's real borrowing and refinancing costs (and raises yields demanded by counterparties), tightening budgetary headroom and delaying or scaling back weapons purchases and foreign deliveries.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
