<edge source="global_bond_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="global_oil_reordering::legal_sanctions_regime_s" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A surge in cross-border capital flows into opaque jurisdictions and intermediaries expands channels for sanctioned actors to receive payments and financing, degrading the coherence and enforceability of legal sanctions frameworks and undermining sanctions effectiveness.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d40">global_oil_reordering</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_procurement_rat" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp reductions in cross-border capital and correspondent banking flows impede payments to foreign suppliers and intermediaries and constrain FX liquidity, causing cancellations/delays in arms contracts and lower procurement rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_financial" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Large outflows and market repricing prompt private banks and intermediaries to de-risk and cut correspondent lines, effectively intensifying financial restrictions on Russian actors beyond formal measures and raising aggregate financial pressure.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="us_china_strategic_rival::geo_tech_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid outflows or a cutoff of cross-border bond financing to a country with key AI supply-chain roles constrains its ability to support foreign partnerships and subsidies, prompting defensive techno‑nationalist measures and export-control responses that raise US–China tech tensions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-12 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_repricing::cross_border_flows" target="us_iran_gulf_escalation::vessel_transit_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A sudden reduction in cross-border capital and trade finance (letters of credit, export finance and short-term shipping credit) curtails available working capital and insurance for tanker and bulk operators, forcing cancellations/delays and reducing the number of commercial transits through the chokepoint.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_repricing</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_escalation</data>
